# lang-rust — Rust developer toolchain (FETCHED-ONLINE, never baked). `rustup`
# itself is already in the baked dev baseline (packages/goodies.list), so this
# pack only adds the dev CLIs around it plus an OPT-IN `mise:rust` runtime
# directive. All members are official-repo; `iictl pack install lang-rust`
# fetches them online and records the resolved set for an exact, reversible
# `iictl pack remove lang-rust`.
#
# rustup-vs-mise coexistence (PROPOSAL §13): the distro's primary Rust toolchain
# manager is the baked `rustup`. The `mise:rust` directive below is OPT-IN for
# users who prefer mise-managed toolchains; mise installs Rust under its own
# user-owned ~/.config/mise + data dir and shims it on PATH ahead of rustup, so
# the two coexist without either clobbering the other. `iictl pack remove
# lang-rust` undoes the `mise use -g rust` directive (the engine runs the inverse
# `mise use -gu rust`); `rustup` stays, being baseline.
#meta:type lang
cargo-edit
cargo-watch
cargo-nextest
sccache

# Opt-in mise-managed Rust runtime (the engine runs `mise use -g rust`; the
# inverse on remove un-sets it). This is a runtime DIRECTIVE only — no shell
# activation line is written here (that belongs to the shell domain).
mise:rust
